          "authorName": "Sergio Alvarez",
          "postDate": "2026-09-05T20:48:27.127Z",
          "content": "<p>I've tried the synthetic volume idea for ~2 weeks with no clear improvement in my scores, so I dropped it. Still, it would be cool to see this strategy work here, as it helped improve a little in the CZII competition. (Polnet was used there: <a href=\"https://github.com/anmartinezs/polnet\" target=\"_blank\">https://github.com/anmartinezs/polnet</a>)</p>\n<p>I suggest to send DaXi microscope paper as reference (<a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-022-01417-2\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-022-01417-2</a>)</p>\n<p>Here is one example of synthetic volume I tried to use:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F2221915%2F508c44ad1c064184a3a589b7de41f5dd%2Fsynthetic_z_stack_optimized.gif?generation=1788641223173538&amp;alt=media\" alt=\"\"></p>",
